          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong cartesian closed category
            (sometimes:
            = succeed ")" do
              %strong ccc
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+products"} finite products
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            with respect to its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+monoidal+category"} cartesian monoidal structure
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [S,X]
            in a cartesian closed category is often called
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+object"} exponentiation
            and is denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi X
                      %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X^S
          %p
            A
            %em cartesian closed functor
            between cartesian closed categories
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to D
            that is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product-preserving+functor"} product-preserving
            and that is also
            = succeed "," do
              %em exponential-preserving
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a^b) \to F(a)^{F(b)},
          %p corresponding to the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≅
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi a
                    %mi b
                  %mo ×
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi eval
                        %mrow
                          %mi a
                          %mo ,
                          %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(a^b) \times F(b) \cong F(a^b \times b) \stackrel{F(eval_{a, b})}{\to} F(a),
          %p is an isomorphism.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos"} topos
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasitopos"} quasitopos
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              %p
                See also
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+structure+on+presheaves"} closed monoidal structure on presheaves
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                is also cartesian closed. (Cf. e.g. p. 98 of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Categories+Work"} Mac Lane
                = succeed ".)" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Category+Theory+in+Context"} Riehl
            %li
              %p
                Many
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nice+category+of+spaces"} nice categories of topological spaces
                are also cartesian closed, particularly the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convenient+category+of+topological+spaces"} convenient categories of spaces
          %h2#some_basic_consequences Some basic consequences
          %p
            A category is cartesian closed if it has finite products and if for any two objects
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            (thought of as a “space of maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "\u201D)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \to Y^X
            and the set of maps
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \times X \to Y
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z
          %p
            There is an evaluation map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_{X, Y}: Y^X \times X \to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X \to Y^X
            under the bijection. Using the naturality, it may be shown that the bijection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(Z, Y^X) \to \hom(Z \times X, Y)
            takes a map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: Z \to Y^X
            to the composite
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mi ϕ
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ev
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z \times X \stackrel{\phi \times 1_X}{\to} Y^X \times X \stackrel{ev_{X, Y}}{\to} Y
          %p
            and the universal property of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            may be phrased thus: given any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo :
                    %mi Z
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi: Z \times X \to Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ϕ
                  %mo :
                  %mi Z
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi: Z \to Y^X
            for which
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ψ
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ev
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Y
                    %mo ∘
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ×
                    %msub
                      %mn 1
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi = ev_{X, Y} \circ (\phi \times 1_X)
          %p
            Taking
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Z
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Z = 1
            (the terminal object), maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \to Y^X
            (or “points” of
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi π
                          %mn 2
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \stackrel{\pi_{2}^{-1}}{\to} 1 \times X \to Y
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y^X
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hom(1, Y^X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo :
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f]: 1 \to Y^X
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ×
                      %msub
                        %mn 1
                        %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mi Y
                    %mi X
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi ev
                        %mrow
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ×
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 2
                  %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi f
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1 \times X \stackrel{[f] \times 1_X}{\to} Y^X \times X \stackrel{ev_{X, Y}}{\to} Y) = (1 \times X \stackrel{\pi_2}{\to} X \stackrel{f}{\to} Y)
          %p
            The following lemma says that the internal evaluation map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ev
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ev_{X, Y}
            indeed behaves as an evaluation map at the level of underlying sets.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Given a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
              and a point
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x: 1 \to X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %msup
                      %mi Y
                      %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi X
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ev
                          %mrow
                            %mi X
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Y
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \stackrel{\langle [f], x \rangle}{\to} Y^X \times X \stackrel{ev_{X, Y}}{\to} Y
            %p
              is the point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mi x
                      %mo :
                      %mn 1
                      %mo →
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f x: 1 \to Y
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p We have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ,
                                %mi x
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                            %msup
                              %mi Y
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi ev
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo ,
                                    %mi Y
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mn 1
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi δ
                                  %mn 1
                            %mn 1
                            %mo ×
                            %mn 1
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ×
                                %mi x
                            %msup
                              %mi Y
                              %mi X
                            %mo ×
                            %mi X
                            %mover
                              %mo →
